        "id": "dw_tap_oct12",
        "origin": "Denver Water TAP, \"Denver Water supply and water use update\", https://www.denverwater.org/tap/denver-water-snowpack-and-water-supply-update",
        "observed_at": "2026-10-12T12:00:00-06:00",
        "content": "As of Oct. 12, 2026, reservoirs were 67% full, versus an average of 90% full for this time. […] Water use Oct. 1 through Oct. 11 was 34% below the five-year average, […] On Aug. 26, 2026, the board amended its Stage 1 drought resolution to prohibit lawn watering as of Oct. 1. […] Customers are reminded of the ban on lawn watering and spray irrigation as of Oct. 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "gazette_oct15",
        "origin": "Denver Gazette, 2026-10-15, https://www.denvergazette.com/2026/10/15/denvers-reservoirs-dwindle-to-two-thirds-capacity/",
        "observed_at": "2026-10-15T12:00:00-06:00",
        "content": "The system's reservoir storage dropped from 72% capacity to 67% in just five weeks. […] Officials warn levels could fall to 55% to 60% before next spring's runoff. […] Typically, levels would be at 85% capacity before the snowmelt begins. […] It would take a snowpack that's more than 150% of normal this winter. […] To put these numbers into perspective, Denver Water's reservoir storage \"bottomed out\" at 50% of the system's capacity in 2003 […] Denver has never implemented Stage 2 drought restrictions, which ban outdoor watering. […] Peaking early at about 58% of normal, an unusually warm March accelerated the melt, […] Denver Water depends on snowpack for a water supply that serves 1.5 million people across the metro,"
      },
      {
        "id": "denver7_aug",
        "origin": "Denver7, August 2026, https://www.denver7.com/news/drought/denver-water-orders-lawn-sprinklers-off-starting-oct-1-as-drought-pushes-reservoir-levels-to-record-lows",
        "observed_at": "2026-08-26T12:00:00-06:00",
        "content": "As of Aug. 24, storage in Denver Water's supply reservoirs sat at 72% full, […] just 95,000 acre-feet — 22% of normal, […] expected to remain off well into spring 2027."
      },
      {
        "id": "dw_resolution",
